{"execute":{"doc":1,"cmd":{"Write":{"PasteMarkdown":{"text":"Harbour & Finch Architects\n\n14 Quay Street · Bristol BS1 4DJ · +44 117 496 0321 · studio@harbourfinch.example\n\n12 March 2026\n\nMs Eleanor Whitcombe\n\nDirector of Estates\n\nRiverside Arts Trust\n\n2 Canal Walk\n\nBath BA2 3QZ\n\nDear Ms Whitcombe,\n\n**Proposal for the Riverside Gallery extension**\n\nThank you for meeting us at the gallery last week and for showing us the old boat store. We left with a clear sense of what the Trust needs: a light, flexible exhibition space that opens onto the towpath without losing the character of the existing building.\n\nEnclosed is our proposal. It sets out a phased approach that keeps the gallery open throughout construction, a timber-frame structure that meets your carbon target, and a fixed fee for the design stages through to planning.\n\nWe would welcome the chance to present the scheme to the trustees on 2 April. In the meantime, please call me directly on the number above if anything needs clarifying.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDaniel Okafor\n\nPartner, Harbour & Finch Architects\n\nEnclosure: Riverside Gallery extension — design proposal (12 pages)\n"}}}}}
